Mouse scroll wheel still outputs scroll event even after remapping
=====

When I want to remap Wheel Up event it adds the event on top of it instead of overwriting it, which sadly means that the scroll wheel cannot be suppressed!

This is especially annoying because I have my media volume up/down set to scroll+side button and when I use the macro it scrolls content anyway. Any fixes to this?

-----

Mouse wheels often have 2 outputs: a normal and HI_RES.
The simplest solution would be to add a mapping which disables the REL_WHEEL or REL_WEEHL_HI_RES.

Wheel+side button -> your mapping
Wheel HI RES+side button -> disable

